WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.538
Dynamic groups take away the ticket queue,

2
00:00:02.538 --> 00:00:05.950
and with it the human check, so
it's worth naming the dangers.

3
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.531
Whoever can write an attribute
controls the access it grants,

4
00:00:09.531 --> 00:00:12.200
so only the provisioning
service writes them.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.253
A rule edit can remove
hundreds of people at once,

6
00:00:15.253 --> 00:00:18.612
so validate, shadow and pilot
it under change control.

7
00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:22.272
Rules need guards against
disabled accounts and guests,

8
00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:25.463
codes instead of names, and
a plan for empty values.

9
00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:30.837
Removal is slow and doesn't revoke tokens,
so urgent cases disable and revoke.

10
00:00:30.837 --> 00:00:32.862
And watch the membership deltas.

11
00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:34.490
Then, the limits.
